## Per-competitor execution skills

One skill per competitor — runs the use-case against that competitor and produces the raw output to feed into `uc-run--register-competitor-answers`.

### uc-run--competitor--normain

- drive Normain (own product) against `<uc>` structure + `data-sources/`
- emit raw answers → hand off to register skill
- capture `instructions.md` used

### uc-run--competitor--claude

- run questions via Claude API w/ `data-sources/` attached
- model + system prompt pinned per run
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--claude-code

- spawn Claude Code session in a sandbox w/ `data-sources/` mounted
- feed questions, collect responses
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--claude-cowork

- drive Claude Cowork flow against `<uc>`
- manual vs scripted? (likely manual paste step)
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--chatgpt-thinking

- run via ChatGPT (Thinking mode) — likely manual paste loop
- capture prompts + responses
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--m365-copilot

- M365 Copilot — manual run, data-sources uploaded to OneDrive/SharePoint?
- capture how sources were exposed
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--gemini-dr

- Gemini Deep Research — kick off research task, wait for report
- map report → per-question answers
- emit raw answers

### uc-run--competitor--notebooklm

- upload `data-sources/` to a NotebookLM notebook
- ask each question, collect responses
- emit raw answers

